# d3d11_gsso_probe on winoracle (Windows 11, WARP), x64; x86 prints the same.
# Build: x86_64-w64-mingw32-gcc -O0 -static -I tools/oracle_probe
#        -o gsso.exe tools/oracle_probe/d3d11_gsso_probe.c -ld3d11 -ldxgi -luuid
# Lines starting with # are not probe output.
#
# Two WARP behaviours Vitreo deliberately does not reproduce (the D3D11.3
# functional spec says otherwise; 12 diff lines on Vitreo):
#  - [streams] "CreateGeometryShader (no SO): stream 0 rasterized", row 1:
#    WARP rasterizes stream 1 too. A multi-stream GS made without a
#    stream-output declaration rasterizes stream 0 (13.5.2).
#  - the five "GS after the DS" sorted-hash lines ([indirect] x2, [tess] x3):
#    the GS writes its SV_PrimitiveID; WARP hands it a running number per
#    tessellated primitive, Vitreo the patch's id (11.7.9.1: every primitive
#    a patch makes carries that patch's SV_PrimitiveID). The primitive
#    counts match.
